 "open_polygons": [],
 "notes": "Lines on this map (1975 height and bulk, sheet 2H): thin lines about 3 px wide close each block on its own, with blank street paper between blocks; heavy lines about 6-7 px wide are height/bulk district borders. Here the heavy borders run in the street just beside a block's thin outline (beside the OS park block at x 3340-3347 and x 3580-3587; between the rows at y 3400-3410 from x 2960 to 3700; in the alley at x 2896-2900, y 3400-3505; at x 3575-3580, y 3655-3820; along the box's left edge at x 2762-2767 from y 3825 down) and also step through blocks along lot lines. A block outline is told from a border by its width (the border is about twice as heavy) and because it closes one rectangle, while a border carries on across blocks and streets. Corners sit on the outer edge of each block's thin line, read off the 4x ruled close-ups and confirmed with ink-run printouts along rows and columns near each corner. Judgment calls: (1) blocks crossed by stepped heavy borders are typed as one block each, as no thin line is visible under the border: x 2904-2948 at y 3505; x 2972-3072 at y 3505-3540; x 3097-3125 y 3520-3580; x 3228-3700 at y 3450-3475; x 3277-3298 y 3510-3580 (loop); row y 3590-3735 at x 3148-3700; row y 3765-3918 at y 3795-3845. (2) The OS park (x 3353-3575, y 3066-3399) has its own thin outline and is typed as one block; the heavy notch at x 3397-3447, y 3343-3405 lies inside it. (3) The block at the left edge (x 2760-2826, y 3055-3386) has a small jog in its right side at x 2819-2824, y 3212-3236 where the cross street meets it; typed with the jog. (4) At the box's left edge the right line of a block outside the box shows at x 2760-2762, y 3583-3722: typed as a 2 px sliver block; at y 3762-3959 the same kind of line sits under the heavy border at x 2761-2767 and is not typed (at most 2 px labelled street). (5) Lettering touching block lines (130-E at x 3125-3170, y 3640-3800; the 65 at x 3255-3300, y 3880-3970; HEMLOCK, FERN, AUSTIN, ST.) is ignored; corners follow the thin lines. (6) The top row of blocks is cut by the box at y 3020 and shows only 11-27 px; typed. The strip x 3696-3699 at the right edge is street paper.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (AI), 2026-11-23: blocks chosen by eye on ruled close-ups; each corner then set on the outer edge of the block's thin line from the scan's dark-pixel runs (throwaway script), odd measurements checked by hand; checked on the labels picture"
